rom one block of dark warm charcoal-grey stone, 4m wide, its back 5.5m above the dais, with two broad vermilion-and-bronze cloud-scroll bands and thick square armrests; the seat is EMPTY. On the dais at the front LEFT and front RIGHT corners, two cast bronze dragons coiled upright on round drum pedestals, 3m tall, bodies wound in one big S, heads raised and facing forward, chunky simplified forms, warm aged bronze with brown-green patina. PROPORTIONS: FRONT and BACK views about 1.7 times as wide as tall; LEFT and RIGHT views about 1.0 times as wide as tall.",
